          "english_quote": "You might reasonably be moderately indignant with the uneducated over such beliefs.",
          "issue": "The main rendering defensibly attaches μετρίως to indignation, but its note presents that attachment without disclosing the material alternative: μετρίως can qualify εὔλογον, limiting the justification for indignation rather than its intensity. The immediately adjacent wording supports considering that alternative. This is interpretive ambiguity, not evidence of source corruption.",
          "suggested_revision": "Retain the defensible main wording if desired, but expand the note: “The main text takes μετρίως with ἀγανακτεῖν, expressing restrained indignation in the contrast between uneducated and educated people. Alternatively, it may qualify εὔλογον: ‘You might be moderately justified in being indignant with the uneducated over such beliefs.’ On that reading, the qualification concerns the justification rather than the intensity of indignation.” The revised note requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
